-- the reference meaning of a body: what it evaluates to in an environment of values, with no wires,
-- no memory and no sharing. A value is a number, a closure (a body and its environment), or an
-- environment (empty, or a value before an environment); nkd-bad is a number applied, a closure
-- incremented, or the count of steps run out
data NkV = nkd-num (m : Word) | nkd-clo (b : NkTm) (e : NkV) | nkd-nil | nkd-cons (v : NkV) (r : NkV) | nkd-bad
